Bland-Altman for total sleep time (gradient boosting): bias
{{v:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/bland_altman/tst_min/bias:1}} min, 95 % limits of agreement
{{v:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/bland_altman/tst_min/loa_low:0}} to {{v:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/bland_altman/tst_min/loa_high:0}} min
([`results/figures/`](../results/figures/)).

**What the v1 numbers say.**

- On average, the model gets a night's total sleep time much closer than the
  trivial rule (which assumes no wake at all), and its group-level bias is
  small. For a single night, however, the error can exceed two hours.
- Wake detection is the weak point: the model finds about
  {{pct:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/wake_sensitivity:0}} % of wake epochs.
- Logistic regression beat gradient boosting on this test set for total
  sleep time, although gradient boosting was clearly better in internal
  cross-validation (kappa {{p:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/internal_cv/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} vs
  {{p:sleep_wake/models/logistic_regression/internal_cv/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}}). We kept the model chosen before the test was
  run. The gap suggested that internal cross-validation, which mixed the
  training databases, overstated transfer; v2 therefore selects by
  cross-dataset validation instead.
- Apnea minutes transfer poorly. Internal cross-validation kappa
  {{p:apnea/models/gradient_boosting/internal_cv/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} drops to
  {{p:apnea/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} on UCDDB. Part of this is model error and
  part is that the two databases define an "apnea minute" differently.
- Three- and four-stage results are clearly above chance but far from
  clinical staging (REM recall
  {{p:wake_nrem_rem/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/recall_rem:2}}, deep-sleep recall
  {{p:four_class/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/recall_deep:2}}).

### 3.2 v2: selection on training data, one test on HMC

**Protocol.** [`docs/v2_protocol.md`](v2_protocol.md) was written before any
v2 experiment. It fixed the test sets (HMC, never used before, as the primary
test; UCDDB as a labeled second look), the candidate changes (more CAP
records, longer-context features, temporal smoothing, ensembles, class
weighting, event-derived apnea labels from MIT-BIH) and the selection rule:

- Candidates are compared **only on the training databases**, by
  cross-dataset cross-validation (train on CAP, evaluate on MIT-BIH; and the
  reverse). This is a closer proxy for a new hospital than v1's mixed folds.
- Staging metric: mean cross-dataset sleep/wake kappa. A candidate is only
  accepted if its cross-dataset total-sleep-time error is at most
  {{v:v2_test_results/spec/rule/tst_guard:1}} times v1's; candidates within {{v:v2_test_results/spec/rule/tie_margin:2}} kappa of the best go to the
  simplest. The same specification is used for 3 and 4 classes.
- Apnea: the same scheme between Apnea-ECG and MIT-BIH event-derived minute
  labels, with apnea-minute error as the guard.

**Selection result (training data only;
[`docs/v2_selection.md`](v2_selection.md)).** {{len:v2_v2_selection/staging/ranking}} staging specifications
(including the v1 reference) and {{len:v2_v2_selection/apnea/ranking}} apnea specifications were scored.

| | v2 choice | v1 reference |
|---|---|---|
| Staging specification | `{{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/chosen/name}}` | `{{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/v1_reference/name}}` |
| Cross-dataset sleep/wake kappa | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/chosen/xds_sw_kappa:3}} | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/v1_reference/xds_sw_kappa:3}} |
| Cross-dataset total sleep time MAE (min) | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/chosen/xds_tst_mae_min:1}} | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/v1_reference/xds_tst_mae_min:1}} |
| Cross-dataset wake-bout MAE | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/chosen/xds_awakenings_mae:1}} | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/v1_reference/xds_awakenings_mae:1}} |
| Cross-dataset 3-class / 4-class kappa | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/chosen/xds_3class_kappa:3}} / {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/chosen/xds_4class_kappa:3}} | {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/ranking/17/xds_3class_kappa:3}} / {{v:v2_v2_selection/staging/ranking/17/xds_4class_kappa:3}} |
